27d8bfe67231654d8ad592e94c1f12a","event_uuid":"45b14a37-a9ae-43d9-bcf2-b0410c891828","position":{"commit_sha":"1763928eed5a46416bd539dd3cc9be5c99a3bb73","position":"1785618465809770001-45b14a37-a9ae-43d9-bcf2-b0410c891828"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"9040cc827cd71cc178751e59116885637c2a5785ddf5e542ee5d734923608b76","event_uuid":"63b196cf-d015-4e0b-b6ec-6a809bc2c643","position":{"commit_sha":"598f48724787ff80488b4536480a51780d84020c","position":"1785627926765889001-63b196cf-d015-4e0b-b6ec-6a809bc2c643"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Measured evidence from CI wall-clock investigation (Gerrit Verified gate) — adds a THIRD partial-clone site this epic should cover, plus hard numbers for the reclaim case.\n\n## Site not yet in file_impact: gerrit-verify.yaml's verify-identity job\n\nfile_impact currently lists .github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml for the checkout filter. The SAME full-history fetch exists in .github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml, job 'verify-identity', step 'Mount the tickets store (FULL history for commit-ancestry era scoping)' — a bare 'git fetch' with a comment explicitly rejecting --depth. (The sibling 'require-ticket' job in the same file already uses --depth=1, so only this one is full.)\n\n## Measured cost (run 30569775555, 2026-07-30)\n\nJob total 7.3m, of which:\n  - 6.73m  Mount the tickets store (the fetch)\n  - 0.08m  the actual 'rebar verify-identity' invocation\nSo 92% of the job is the clone. The check itself is ~5 seconds because identity.require_authenticated = false (rebar.toml:105) puts it in advisory mode, which short-circuits all git work at verify_authorship.py:532 before any commit map is built.\n\n## Local measurements of the tickets branch (fetched from the GitHub mirror)\n\n  full fetch          66.2s   1.4 GB   51,575 commits\n  --filter=blob:none   3.6s    22 MB\n  + worktree add       8.6s    83 MB  (materializes HEAD blobs only)\n\n18x faster, 64x smaller for the fetch; ~12s total end-to-end vs 66s locally (6.73m on a GH runner).\n\n## The stated blocker does NOT apply\n\nThe step comment justifies the full fetch as needed for 'merge-base / commit-ancestry scoping against identity.enforce_since'. A blob:none partial clone keeps the COMPLETE commit graph — only blobs are lazy. Verified directly on the partial clone:\n\n  git merge-base --is-ancestor 0cf8c03530d379991933740d9e4d1fa46ce4484a refs/remotes/gh-tickets  -> exit 0\n\nSo the era-scoping requirement is fully preserved. Note --depth/shallow would NOT be safe here: _is_enforced (verify_authorship.py:299-319) fails CLOSED on any git error, so a truncated graph turns grandfathered events into enforced ones and produces spurious failures. blob:none avoids that entirely because the graph is intact.\n\n## Why this matters for the reclaim story (0303)\n\nThe 1.4 GB / 51,575-commit figure is the direct measurement of the growth 0303 is trying to bound — every ticket event is an auto-commit. Partial clone is the mitigation; it does not shrink the branch. Both are worth doing: blob:none makes CI cheap NOW regardless of how long the reclaim takes to land.\n\n## Caveat on _collect_all under blob:none\n\nIn ENFORCED mode (require_authenticated = true) _collect_all reads every active event file at HEAD, which the worktree checkout already materializes — that is the 83 MB above, not a lazy-fetch storm. But the introducing-commit map (authorship.build_introducing_commit_map, a --full-history git log pass) should be re-measured on a partial clone before enforcement is re-flipped, since a name-only log over 51k commits may fault in trees. Not a blocker for landing the filter while the gate is advisory.\n\nSource: CI wall-clock reduction investigation. Not claiming this ticket — filing the evidence.","timestamp":1785438354619009001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Execution started under rebar-implement in worktree impl-42eb-tickets-clone; session log dc9a-ea86-ecba-40a0. Plan-review PASS and epic claimed. Accepted review advisories will be enforced at leaf level: caller-safe None behavior for B4, exact fallback resolvers for B5, and B6 before B1 alongside the existing B3 before B1 edge. Gerrit fallback is sequential refs/for/main because this identity is not a feature-branch-driver.","timestamp":1785599404536470001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation continuation moved to fresh worktree impl-42eb-tickets-clone-v2 at landed B1 SHA 16a1a385b8 because Gerrit rebased the submitted commit. Session trail continues in session_log 06ff-678a-3f46-4ea7; prior milestones remain in dc9a-ea86-ecba-40a0.","timestamp":1785618465809770001}],"created_at":1785372080361335001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a254c9c2-b87d-4cdf-a27c-422d4cce5cb0","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1270-b740-92c0-4b46"},{"link_uuid":"6f543de5-9f35-436f-ae2c-2af03052c95d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1cb6-d553-6565-49b4"},{"link_uuid":"5631cc94-81ce-4550-8946-2e59291febac","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"01e8-302b-ab8f-4220"},{"link_uuid":"91cebe18-7eaa-457e-bd21-8934a1c7946a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f3d4-c062-31e4-4713"},{"link_uuid":"ab395ac7-72c7-4084-bd00-39ddb7b67c4e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"dc9a-ea86-ecba-40a0"},{"link_uuid":"7d0660bc-55ce-4f8b-9012-9d52fab25184","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"06ff-678a-3f46-4ea7"},{"link_uuid":"63b196cf-d015-4e0b-b6ec-6a809bc2c643","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"d788-7020-7c13-4050"}],"description":"Cut the cost of obtaining the tickets store, and fix the fail-open bootstrap that silently\nproduces an empty divergent store.\n\nMeasured facts and the corrected premises: session_log **1cb6-d553-6565-49b4**\n(dinky-frowsy-woodborer). Sibling epic: **0303-692c** (censual-organic-mouflon). Umbrella:\n**1270-b740**.\n\n## Context\n\nA fresh full clone of `tickets` costs **1.04 GiB / 59s wall / 319s CPU**. Measured against GitHub,\n`--filter=blob:none` costs **68.7 MiB / 14.3s** — a ~15x reduction. In CI the tickets objects arrive\nin the `actions/checkout` step, measured at **237 s** on run 30494781536, versus **2 s** for the\nmanual worktree mount that follows.\n\nSeparately, P1 bug **01e8-302b** (bilingual-capitalist-caecilian) is open: in Claude Code's web\nenvironment the tickets fetch timed out through the agent git proxy and `rebar init` **silently\nbootstrapped a fresh empty store**, diverging from `origin/tickets` so every read returned `[]` and\nnew writes landed on a branch that cannot fast-forward back.\n\n## Approach and why this one\n\n**rebar cannot filter a clone it does not perform.** `grep -rn 'git clone' src/` yields only a\ndocstring; every rebar fetch is post-clone, and `init.py:375` runs only inside `if remote:` — i.e.\nonly once `origin/tickets` already resolves, by which point the objects are local. So the size lever\nis the `actions/checkout` step (which has supported a `filter:` input since v4.1.0) plus documented\nclone guidance — not rebar-side fetch flags. This is a deliberate narrowing after two earlier\ndesigns were measured to be inert.\n\n`blob:none` is safe for rebar's own access patterns: whole-store `verify-identity` in a blobless\nclone fetched **0 bytes** and ran *faster* than in a full clone (3.75s vs 3.98s), because its scan is\na pure tree-level diff and event/keyring bodies are read from the **working tree**\n(`verify_authorship.py:371`, `authorship.py:119-128`). The accepted cost is stated rather than\nwaved away: `git blame` over historical trees runs on the bug-close path\n(`metrics/blame.py:69` <- `derive_caused_by` <- `transition_close.py:513`).\n\nAnd a faster fetch does **not** fix the P1 — it only lowers the probability. The mechanism is the\nfail-open fallthrough to `worktree add --orphan`, which is fixed directly.\n\n## Scope (children)\n\n1. **B3** set `merge.ours.driver=true` in the reconciler workflow (prerequisite for B1)\n2. **B1** add `filter: blob:none` to the `actions/checkout` steps that mount tickets\n3. **B2** fail closed instead of orphan-bootstrapping an empty store (fixes P1 01e8-302b)\n4. **B4** clone guidance doc + make `derive_caused_by` abort on any per-path blame failure\n5. **B5** add `--no-renames` and `-c log.showSignature=false` to the two authorship resolvers\n6. **B6** delete `.bridge_state.bak-retarget` (33,025,572 bytes sitting in the tree at HEAD)\n\n## Compatibility and rollback\n\nEvery child is independently revertible and none changes a persisted format. B3 must land **before**\nB1: `reconcile-bridge.yml` uses `fetch-depth: 0` precisely because shallow history breaks merge-base,\nand `blob:none` keeps commits but removes merge-base **blobs** which the reconverge path\nmaterializes — with `merge.ours.driver` undefined on the runner, `.bridge_state/* merge=ours`\nsilently degrades to a 3-way text merge of an 18 MB JSON file. B6 must land before epic\n0303-692c's reclaim so the strip does not retain those blobs.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A controlled **before/after byte measurement** (pack size, or `GIT_TRACE_PACKET` received\n      bytes) of a fresh CI checkout with and without the filter shows the expected reduction, **and**\n      the subsequent manual tickets fetch is confirmed to inherit\n      `remote.origin.partialclonefilter`. Must NOT be a config-presence assertion: git writes that\n      key even when the server ignored the filter (reproduced). Tier: CI job measurement.\n- [ ] A reconverge against a diverged remote succeeds on a blobless runner (proves B3 landed before\n      B1 and the merge driver is defined).\n- [ ] With a reachable remote advertising `tickets`, a simulated fetch failure causes a **non-zero\n      exit** and **no orphan branch is created**. Tier: CLI subprocess against a real temporary\n      remote. This is the RED case for P1 01e8-302b.\n- [ ] `derive_caused_by` returns `None` when blame fails on **any** path, rather than tallying a\n      partial path set and electing a culprit that would not have won over the full set (which would\n      write a wrong `caused_by` link). Tier: unit test injecting a per-path failure, asserting no\n      link event is written.\n- [ ] With `log.showSignature=true` **and signed commits** in the fixture repo, `resolve_event_commit`\n      and `resolve_position_commit` return a valid 40-hex SHA. The signing is load-bearing: with\n      `--format=%H` over unsigned commits the setting emits no extra lines, so an unsigned fixture\n      makes this vacuously green. Tier: unit against a real temporary git repo.\n- [ ] `.bridge_state.bak-retarget` is absent from the tree at HEAD and working-tree size drops by\n      >=33 MB.\n- [ ] The clone-guidance doc exists and states the measured numbers (full 1.04 GiB / 59s vs\n      blob:none 68.7 MiB / 14.3s) and the accepted `git blame` degradation.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":".github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml","reason":"checkout filter + merge.ours.driver"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/init.py","reason":"fail closed instead of orphan bootstrap"},{"path":"src/rebar/attest/authorship.py","reason":"--no-renames + log.showSignature on both resolvers"},{"path":"src/rebar/metrics/blame.py","reason":"abort derive_caused_by on any per-path blame failure"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","01e8-302b-ab8f-4220"],["relates_to","06ff-678a-3f46-4ea7"],["relates_to","1270-b740-92c0-4b46"],["relates_to","1cb6-d553-6565-49b4"],["relates_to","d788-7020-7c13-4050"],["relates_to","dc9a-ea86-ecba-40a0"],["relates_to","f3d4-c062-31e4-4713"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"7203c03b-eb1a-442c-a4a6-5544a5ab59a9","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"42eb-5789-c798-4dfc","ticket_type":"epic","title":"Cut tickets-store clone cost via CI partial clone + fail closed instead of bootstrapping an empty store","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["45bd2d68-d9d2-4ea9-858b-b7766f4b623d","a254c9c2-b87d-4cdf-a27c-422d4cce5cb0","6f543de5-9f35-436f-ae2c-2af03052c95d","5631cc94-81ce-4550-8946-2e59291febac","6d7c0eaf-aa99-412d-9f6b-d929f879180b","5ab34f15-d5ef-43cb-bba4-3a158bb5ee4a","91cebe18-7eaa-457e-bd21-8934a1c7946a","ab395ac7-72c7-4084-bd00-39ddb7b67c4e","047c11df-a543-41bf-80ac-b9e888d93a97","7203c03b-eb1a-442c-a4a6-5544a5ab59a9","3802c44c-97c8-4087-949d-35f6cbfa002a","784724d9-fd43-4b29-83b2-0298c3898d96","7d0660bc-55ce-4f8b-9012-9d52fab25184","45b14a37-a9ae-43d9-bcf2-b0410c891828","63b196cf-d015-4e0b-b6ec-6a809bc2c643"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785627926765889002,"uuid":"2b2675ef-6976-40ff-91b0-860593ca59d2"}